    "design": "0015, SWM-1"
  },
  "formats": {
    "reference": "freedom-browser at meta.freedomBrowserCommit (integration/rust-core, with #1057 and #1062), its main-process modules loaded whole, over meta.packages: bee-js 13.2.0 and core-sdk 0.2.2 exactly. meta.files is every installed package file the run loaded (Node's require cache, the GSOC workers' included: bee-js, core-sdk, cafe-utility, ethers, better-sqlite3's JavaScript, isomorphic-ws and the rest) and each such package's package.json, keyed <name>@<version>/<path>, by SHA-256; a package whose native addon the run loaded has every addon it ships digested (better-sqlite3's prebuilds, each platform's), so the list is the same on any machine. Electron, the identity core (core/vault-backend.js), identity-manager.js's own lower modules (profile paths, the node identity guard, the Radicle gate, private files), the grant mirror, the service registry, the publish setup service and the vault timer are the world each case scripts (generator/swarm-world.js); identity-manager.js itself is the reference's, so its texts (a locked vault's, a bad publisher index's) are its own.",
    "content": "content(seed, n): SHA-256(seed ‖ u64_be(i)) for i = 0, 1, …, concatenated and cut to n bytes. A data spec is { utf8 }, { hex }, { base64 } or { seed, length }.",
    "keys": "every signature is core-sdk's, under keys.json's abandon-12 Bee wallet and publisher keys (public test keys: never fund them).",
    "clock": "Date.now() is the case's clock (ms) for the whole run, a step's own clock from that step on.",
    "node_url": "the node is a recording fake on loopback; every text names it http://127.0.0.1:1633, or a session's node_url.",
    "typed": "params and non-JSON answers: { string }, { string_json } (a string with a lone surrogate, as its JSON text), { string_repeat, count }, { number: String(n) } (\"-0\", \"NaN\", \"Infinity\"), { bigint }, { boolean }, { null }, { undefined }, { array } ({ hole } for a hole), { object: [[key, value], …] } in key order; where a method reads data, { bytes, kind, base64 } or { string_bytes, base64 } (a string's UTF-8), past 64 KiB { …, part: i } with parts[i] = { seed | repeat+count, length, sha256 }; { bytes_elsewhere, kind, base64 } for bytes where no method reads them; in answers, { string_digest: units, sha256 } for a string past 8,192 units. An answer is `result` or `error` when JSON keeps it exactly, else `result_typed` or `error_typed`; a JSON result past 16 KiB is `result_digest` { json_length, sha256 }.",
    "methods": "a case: its world (origin, the page key; grants, the Swarm grants by key, their autoApprove the site's rules; feeds, swarm-feeds.json's text before or null; vault, the identity core's, which an approved vault.unlock prompt opens; at_execute, the world's changes as the dispatcher hands the request to the service, after its checks (vault: locked, the auto-lock firing; custody; rule_off; name: moved; messaging, connection or feed_access: revoked, the user's Settings meanwhile); readiness, getPublishReadiness()'s answer or \"throws\"; custody, whether the agent holds the tab (Agent custody, read live); prompts, the scripted answers in order ({ kind, approve, choices } or { kind, closed }), a prompt with none approved with its default choices (a feed prompt's active identity, or its new one where the prompt doesn't offer the active one; \"always allow\" off); keyless, a document with no key; identity_wallet: false, the Identity & Wallet switch off (settings.json); grants_unavailable, the grant mirror unloaded; manifest, a bzz: document's freedom-manifest.json, which main's manifest check fetches through the bzz: handler (an https: or ens: document's check answers legacy, with no fetch); session, a subscribe-proxy case's; node, the fake node's declarative state; clock) and its steps. A step goes through main's page dispatcher (src/main/page/page-swarm.js, createSwarmDispatchers, loaded whole) with page-requests.js's context scripted: the requester attested (one guest, window, frame and navigation, so a case's steps are one document's), its PageContext, the prompts, the name holding unless the world moves it. Only the dispatcher's UI and core boundaries are injected: the guest's webContents (live, on the default session), Agent custody (the world's) and the setup screen; its hand-off to executeSwarmMethod is observed, never changed. Everything else (the grants through swarm-permissions.js, the manifest check, the feed store, the origin lock, the vault's state through identity-manager.js, settings) is main's own. A step with page: false calls executeSwarmMethod(method, params, origin) directly, with no meta: a method page-requests.js has no row for (it answers those itself, design 0011) and the service's own no-page guards. Each step records the answer, every node request (via fetch or http; method, path, query pairs, the headers the caller set, the body as { bytes, base64 } up to 8 KiB else { bytes, sha256 }, the status, feed { owner, index } for a feed update's address, and the grammar's verdict: form, ready or deviation), and its events in order: the approval path (custody, each read of Agent custody when a rule could answer; prompt { kind, view, answer }; service { key, page, approval }, what the dispatcher handed executeSwarmMethod: the key, a page's meta, how main approved a SOC, auto for the site's rule or user for its prompt; effect { custody, outcome: ran | refused }, the guard just before the effect, with its custody reads when a rule answered; world, a change the case scripts), the identity core's calls (grant, revoke, touch: the grant mirror's writes; sign_soc: the request, its PageContext and authorization), readiness (after_requests node requests in), vault_timer_reset, route_to_setup, page_event (connect) and delivered (a subscription's message), manifest_fetch. `after`: swarm-feeds.json's text, its backups, the publish history (getEntries()), and for a manifest case swarm-manifest-grants.json's text. A case marked deviation records the reference's outcome, and `core` the design's.",
    "session": "subscribe-proxy's world (design 0015, question 4): proxy and tor (on or off), node_kind, node_url (the node main's service registry names; a remote one's calls reach the fake node), node_loopback (main's own isLoopbackGatewayUrl over it, as bzz:'s transport classifies the Ant node) and subscribe_check, main's answer to the core's subscribe check (shell.swarm_ready), the core's input: { ok: false, reason: proxy-or-tor } while a proxy or Tor is on and the node isn't on loopback, else { ok: true }. The reference reads none of it and opens the socket either way (`websockets`), which is the deviation; where the check answers ok it is parity.",
    "node": "stamps, addresses, tags, node: JSON answers (stamps_label_bytes: the usable batch with a label of that many bytes of l); data: blobs stored as their whole ChunkSplitter tree and joined from /bytes; chunks: raw bytes at an address; entries: feed updates, SOCs signed under the named test key ({ key, topic (the topic string), index, data, wrap }); latest: GET /feeds/<o>/<t>'s reply; probes: the feeds whose updates 0 to head exist (a hit answers 105 zero bytes); probeFail: one index's status; rules: replies tried first, { match: { method, path | prefix }, reply: { status, statusText, headers, json | body_utf8 | body_hex | body_base64 | body_data, chunked + pieces_data (each piece reaches the reader as one frame, whatever the socket's reads), cutAfterPieces, declare (a Content-Length longer than the body, then the connection cut), hangUp, delayMs, abortPage (the page gives up as this request arrives: the request's signal aborts) }, world (a change to the case's world as the request arrives: custody, rule_off, name) }. Unmatched, the node answers from what it stores: 404 { code, message } for what it lacks, /bzz with SHA-256 of the body as its reference.",
    "bodies": "write-side.json's shapes: tar (page-upload.js's, for window.swarm, each equal to bee-js's collection upload of the same entries; tar-paths cases are bee-js's publishCollection, as freedom://publish uses it), file (publishData's request; the body is the data), bytes (a large feed entry's POST /bytes body, ChunkSplitter's root of it and the SOC upload body that wraps that root), soc (core-sdk), chunk (POST /chunks: span ‖ payload and the address), pss (the request; the body is the message).",
    "trees": "core-sdk's ChunkSplitter: root, span, root payload, and every chunk's count and SHA-256 over address ‖ u64_le(span) ‖ payload by address.",
    "stamps": "mapped: bee-js's stamp.getAll over one raw batch (the fields Freedom reads, or the error), and swarm-service.js's classification; select: selectBestBatch(size, options) over a /stamps answer, its batch or error, and how many /stamps reads it made; where it made two, deviation stamps-one-read, and `core` gives the core's one read, with the same batch or error. A mapped batch with a fractional depth or bucketDepth is deviation batch-depth: `core` is the core's refusal.",
    "feeds": "topic and identifier (bee-js), update (feed-service.js's updateFeed and writeFeedPayload, write-side.json's shape), index_run and entry_exists (from the methods that ran them), metered_read (readFeedPayload over a recording meter: each charge and reserve, refused or not).",
    "gsoc": "bee-js's gsocMine (write-side.json's shape): the signer's index, key, owner and SOC address, or its error.",
    "errors": "http_error: a node error at each call site (bee-js's JSON and array-buffer calls, #1057's fetchNode, the SOC upload, page-upload.js): the error's class, message and data, and isChunkNotFoundError (fetchNode at 500, which readFeedPayload reads as an empty feed, and at 503, which reaches its own text); past 8 KiB, `core` is the same reader over the first 8,192 bytes (error-body-bound). mapping: the method cases that show nodeWriteError's and mapChunkReadError's mappings.",
    "stores": "feeds: feed-store.js's operations from a file's text, each result or error, and the files after (backups included); manifests: permission-manifests.js's check, decide, useIndividual, disconnect and get over scripted manifests, the grants and files after; history: publish-history.js's operations (after a first session's, `seeded`, with a BLOB cell written into one of its rows where `blob` says), the schema, pragmas and rows (a BLOB cell as { blob: hex }). Local time is UTC (generate.js sets TZ). A case marked deviation records the reference's outcome, and `core` the core's: index-allocation's as text, history-bound's row count, and for the others what the case records, each answer in the form the case's own take: feeds `ops` (each operation's answer) and `files`; manifests `steps`, `grants_after` and `files`, or `load: unreadable` (the core reads neither the file nor a .bak copy: no step reads the store, and nothing is written); history `ops` and `rows`, with `refused` { reason: blob, column } for a read the core refuses (history-blobs). Where the core's answers are the reference's own over another input, that input is: for store-refusal, the operations but the refused one, whose answer is the reference's refusal; for store-shapes, the feed store as the core holds it (`core_before`, each feed map rebuilt as sanitizeV2OriginEntry does) or a manifest file that doesn't parse, beside the same .bak copy; for legacy-dates, the legacy file with each timestamp the core doesn't take removed."
  },
